                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a09d5474-673a-3c8b-9d06-5ce9edb3ca22",
                        "entry_id": "8c35f2f4-022e-36dd-8a86-56368c336d1a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. (о человеке, животном) имеющий большое пузо, живот"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f214e18-d61c-440d-b56b-bd3ef3e215ba",
                                "sense_id": "a09d5474-673a-3c8b-9d06-5ce9edb3ca22",
                                "text": "Вокруг него [Буратино] собрались обитатели пруда: всем известные своей глупостью чёрные пузатые головастики, водяные жуки с задними лапками, похожими на вёсла, пиявки, личинки, которые кушали всё, что попадалось, вплоть до самих себя, и, наконец, разные мелкие инфузории."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7be059b1-0e7d-3593-bbdb-7b1a0d331e63",
                        "entry_id": "8c35f2f4-022e-36dd-8a86-56368c336d1a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. (о каком-либо сосуде, ёмкости) имеющий форму, близкую к шару"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5248d31c-60c8-4dc8-935a-174ef5bf7714",
                        "source_entry_id": "8c35f2f4-022e-36dd-8a86-56368c336d1a",
                        "target_lang_word": "paunchy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "paunchy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "457d4d7e-980d-3dd2-ba26-bab0b68d9935",
                                        "entry_id": "881d5a78-43b3-3d78-8d5d-c6bc6390f86e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a paunch; having a prominent stomach; potbellied."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a972845d-a7a2-44cc-98e1-49394fecccdb",
                                                "sense_id": "457d4d7e-980d-3dd2-ba26-bab0b68d9935",
                                                "text": "He exercised every day to avoid becoming paunchy in his old age."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f2a7ea7-08a4-490a-934c-02d2ab4275de",
                                                "sense_id": "457d4d7e-980d-3dd2-ba26-bab0b68d9935",
                                                "text": "A trim-middled hog will have a higher dressing percentage than a wasty, gutty, paunchy, heavy-middled hog."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c25e3ec1-ac8e-4a46-8274-a857e141c32f",
                                                "sense_id": "457d4d7e-980d-3dd2-ba26-bab0b68d9935",
                                                "text": "\"They live in New York, and he had the effrontery to give me a dinner and ask all his collaborators to it, fat, paunchy men who smelled of money. Pfaugh!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1b9867a-8d15-4e62-b9ec-88779431af6b",
                                                "sense_id": "457d4d7e-980d-3dd2-ba26-bab0b68d9935",
                                                "text": "\"I don't think personalities change,\" Bill said. \"We get a little paunchier and we get a few wrinkles and a little gray hair. But you have the same personality.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c3083a0-d847-4cde-b7f1-18bd336be86b",
                                                "sense_id": "457d4d7e-980d-3dd2-ba26-bab0b68d9935",
                                                "text": "The National Park Service has capitalized on the increasingly rotund population by live-streaming the hungry bears and creating an online bracket in which 12 of the park’s paunchiest are pitted against one another. Fans vote for their favorite bear in head-to-head matchups until the title of Fattest Bear is bestowed, this year on Tuesday."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "02d1f734-25b1-4127-ae69-f491535be2c1",
                        "source_entry_id": "8c35f2f4-022e-36dd-8a86-56368c336d1a",
                        "target_lang_word": "bellied",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bellied",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc41a703-1885-33ec-a29e-29675fb11410",
                                        "entry_id": "43f4e651-e050-3e41-8f06-a4d560dc0455",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a large or prominent belly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d05c005e-6950-4dcc-b15f-4713d295ed6e",
                                                "sense_id": "dc41a703-1885-33ec-a29e-29675fb11410",
                                                "text": "There was, also, among the company a mannered, bellied person called Alured Castorley […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8bc58090-b862-3f3e-8310-6b42fc8d5772",
                                        "entry_id": "43f4e651-e050-3e41-8f06-a4d560dc0455",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a belly of a specified type."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in-compounds",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5fde186-a8de-4feb-b03c-0908164f9cf3",
                                                "sense_id": "8bc58090-b862-3f3e-8310-6b42fc8d5772",
                                                "text": "full-bellied knife"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a81b881c-39a3-45e7-97db-3a6306f7c48e",
                                                "sense_id": "8bc58090-b862-3f3e-8310-6b42fc8d5772",
                                                "text": "round-bellied vase"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a215f61-e533-422e-88e9-d55ae640ead6",
                                                "sense_id": "8bc58090-b862-3f3e-8310-6b42fc8d5772",
                                                "text": "But one guy was still yelping: a big-bellied biker, with a long, black beard that hung halfway down his bloated gut."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2410159b-51dc-3cab-bc18-76644b385b2d",
                                        "entry_id": "43f4e651-e050-3e41-8f06-a4d560dc0455",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Swollen, bulging, or billowing; bellying."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8184ae3-f3b9-404d-bf1d-50f3f7218fb3",
                                                "sense_id": "2410159b-51dc-3cab-bc18-76644b385b2d",
                                                "text": "1819, Joseph Rodman Drake, “The American Flag” in The Culprit Fay, and Other Poems, New York: Van Norden & King, 1847, p. 91,\nFlag of the seas! on ocean wave\nThy stars shall glitter o’er the brave;\nWhen death, careering on the gale,\nSweeps darkly round the bellied sail,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a94a9ba1-5683-4f61-a7eb-71e3707cc540",
                                                "sense_id": "2410159b-51dc-3cab-bc18-76644b385b2d",
                                                "text": "We heard the swarming streets, the noisy mills;\nSaw sooty foundries full of glare and gloom,\nGreat bellied chimneys tipped with tongues of flame,\nQuiver in smoky heat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40782e06-d044-4a4e-91e9-6638d74eec8d",
                                                "sense_id": "2410159b-51dc-3cab-bc18-76644b385b2d",
                                                "text": "Hand-like rushed the vintage; we strung the bellied skins\nPlump, and at the sealing the Youth’s voice rose:"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad6f08c8-dfe5-38e0-9267-5b217e64fd85",
                                        "entry_id": "43f4e651-e050-3e41-8f06-a4d560dc0455",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Overblown, exaggerated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50b10f78-4fe3-4469-8e24-1fa20b5cd6ba",
                                                "sense_id": "ad6f08c8-dfe5-38e0-9267-5b217e64fd85",
                                                "text": "[…] the choicest of his friends,\nSuch as would blush to talk such serious follies,\nOr back such bellied commendations […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
